 world's strongest software engineering model.\n\nView original source\n\nFan commentary from Devin Central. Devin is a trademark of Cognition.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCognition ships Devin Voice: speak a task, Devin plans and codes · VibeHacker (https://vibehacker.com/news/cognition-ships-devin-voice-speak-a-task-devin-plans-and-codes)\nciteturn781search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 days ago; Crawled: 2 days ago; Product Hunt · Sep 13, 2026 · 5:30 PM ... Devin Voice (Product Hunt #8 on Sept 11) lets you talk through a task so Devin plans, codes, and ships it, using GPT-Live for conversation and Cognition’s SWE-2 model for the engineering.\n\nProduct Hunt · Sep 13, 2026 · 5:30 PM\n\n# Cognition ships Devin Voice: speak a task, Devin plans and codes\n\nDevin Voice (Product Hunt #8 on Sept 11) lets you talk through a task so Devin plans, codes, and ships it, using GPT-Live for conversation and Cognition’s SWE-2 model for the engineering. Docs cover mute, push-to-talk, and interrupting mid-call from the Agent session UI.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCognition Launches Devin Voice — Speak a Task, Devin Ships the Code · FounderMag (https://foundermag.co/launches/devin-voice/)\nciteturn781search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 days ago; Crawled: 4 days ago; By Priya Raman · September 10, 2026 · via Product Hunt ... Cognition launched Devin Voice on Product Hunt on September 10, a voice-controlled interface for Devin, the company’s autonomous AI software engineer.\n\n# Cognition Launches Devin Voice — Speak a Task, Devin Ships the Code\n\nBy Priya Raman · September 10, 2026 · via Product Hunt\n\nImage: Devin Voice Product Hunt launch graphic: \"You say it, Devin ships it\"AI\n\n## What launched\n\nCognition launched Devin Voice on Product Hunt on September 10, a voice-controlled interface for Devin, the company’s autonomous AI software engineer. Instead of typing a task into a chat box, a developer speaks it aloud; the voice layer, powered by OpenAI’s full-duplex GPT-Live model, handles the natural back-and-forth conversation, while Cognition’s own SWE-2 model does the underlying planning, coding, and delivery. The launch team framed it simply: “Speak a task out loud and Devin plans, codes, and delivers.” Devin Voice is free to use, available now at devin.ai, with setup documentation at docs.devin.ai.\n\nRelated Best Tools 7 AI Agent Platforms Worth Building With in 2026\n\n1Relevance AINo-code platform for building and managing teams of AI agents ('AI workforces') that automate business tasks across sales, support, research, and ops.【--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHow to Use Devin Voice (2026 Guide) – AISagely (https://aisagely.com/devin-voice/)\nciteturn781search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 days ago; Crawled: 3 days ago; # How to Use Devin Voice (2026 Guide) ... Cognition announced it on September 10, 2026, running on OpenAI's GPT-Live for the conversation and Cognition's own SWE-2 model for the engineering work underneath.\n\n# How to Use Devin Voice (2026 Guide)\n\nHow-To Guides 8 min read\n\nBy Vishal Swami — Founder & Lead AI Reviewer, AISagely · Updated 2026-09-13\n\nDevin Voice is Cognition's full-duplex voice mode for Devin, its AI software engineer — you click a call button, talk through a task the way you'd brief a coworker, and Devin plans and writes the code while you keep talking. Cognition announced it on September 10, 2026, running on OpenAI's GPT-Live for the conversation and Cognition's own SWE-2 model for the engineering work underneath.\n\n> Short answer: Open a Devin session, click the voice call button beside the message box, and grant microphone access. Talk naturally — you can interrupt Devin mid-sentence, and it can talk back while still working. Voice mode runs inside your normal Devin plan (Free through Enterprise); there's no separate charge just to make the call.\n\nLast updated September 13, 2026.\n\nI've spent the past few days running real tasks through Devin Voice — bug fixes, a small refactor, one \"just go add this endpoint\" request — specifically to see whether talking to an AI software engineer actually saves time over typing, or whether it's a novelty that gets in the way once the task gets specific. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDevin Voice Launched by Cognition: Talk to Your AI Coder | AIToolly (https://aitoolly.com/ai-news/article/2026-09-12-cognition-introduces-devin-voice-on-product-hunt-real-time-spoken-interaction-meets-autonomous-softw)\nciteturn781search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 days ago; Crawled: 4 days ago; Hunting the release, tech figure KP highlighted how the tool bridges natural speech and end-to-end task execution, enabling developers to verbally instruct Devin to plan, write, test, and ship code. ... September 10, 2026 at 10:45 PM ... Devin Voice uses a decoupled dual-model architecture: GPT-Live powers natural, low-latency spoken conversation, while Cognition's new SWE-2 model handles deep code reasoning, software architecture, and execution under the hood.\n\nProduct Launch Devin Cognition AI Voice AI\n\n# Cognition Introduces Devin Voice on Product Hunt: Real-Time Spoken Interaction Meets Autonomous Software Engineering\n\nCognition has introduced Devin Voice on Product Hunt, presenting a real-time conversational voice interface for its flagship autonomous software engineer, Devin. Hunting the release, tech figure KP highlighted how the tool bridges natural speech and end-to-end task execution, enabling developers to verbally instruct Devin to plan, write, test, and ship code. Under the hood, Devin Voice pairs an interactive conversational layer powered by GPT-Live with Cognition's newly debuted SWE-2 frontier coding model. Featuring landline-inspired controls such as interactive calling, push-to-talk shortcuts, muting, and direct barge-in capabilities, Devin Voice establishes an entirely voice-driven paradigm for agentic workflows, moving developer collaboration beyond static prompts toward dynamic verbal pair programming.\n\nSeptember 10, 2026 at 10:45 PM\n\nProduct Hunt\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOn-demand design of controlled-release systems using an expert-mimic AI framework | Nature Communications (https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-026-77619-5)\nciteturn781search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: yesterday; Crawled: today;   * Ying Qin^{1,2}^{ na1}, ... We show that E-MAF delivers on-demand release and shortens design cycles from 6-12 months to approximately 1 hour. ... E-MAF is a framework designed to accelerate the development and clinical translation of polymeric controlled-release systems and drug-delivery technologies.\n\nOn-demand design of controlled-release systems using an expert-mimic AI framework\n\nDownload PDF\n\nDownload PDF\n\n  * Article\n  * Open access\n  * Published: 15 September 2026\n\n# On-demand design of controlled-release systems using an expert-mimic AI framework\n\n  * Ying Qin^{1,2}^{ na1},\n  * Rushuang Zhou^{3}^{ na1},\n  * Yali Ming^{2,4}^{ na1},\n  * Bohao Li  ORCID: orcid.org/0009-0004-0627-806X^{5}^{ na1},\n  * Yuning Hu^{6},\n  * Donglin Sui^{2},\n  * Jingxuan Liu^{2},\n  * Hang Wang^{6},\n  * Guanghui Ma  ORCID: orcid.org/0000-0001-9154-5556^{2,4},\n  * Yuedong Yang  ORCID: orcid.org/0000-0002-6782-2813^{5},\n  * Yining Dong^{1} &\n  * …\n  * Yufei Xia  ORCID: orcid.org/0000-0003-1215-6128^{2,4} \nShow authors\n\nNature Communications (2026)\n\nSave article\n\nView saved research\n\nWe’re sharing this article early to provide faster access to peer-reviewed, accepted research. It is citable and carries a permanent DOI. This version is subject to further edits and will be replaced automatically by the final Version of Record. All legal disclaimers apply.\n\n## Abstract\n\nNavigating a vast formulation-preparation design space that is highly sensitive to perturbations makes trial-and-error approaches inefficient and costly for diverse clinical needs. Here, we introduce an expert-mimic AI framework called E-MAF that integrates a process-aware surrogate with an optimized genetic algorithm to emulate coarse-to-fine reasoning, autonomously generating lab-ready designs tailored to desired release profiles. We show that E-MAF delivers on-demand release and shortens design cycles from 6-12 months to approximately 1 hour. We demonstrate that in vitro release, in vivo pharmacokinetics and therapeutic effects match or surpass commercial benchmarks across 7 active pharmaceutical ingredients. We show that E-MAF also enables release profiles that are hard to achieve by conventional approaches, exemplified by ≤2% risperidone burst within 1 h and near-zero-order release over ~28 days in vivo. These results demonstrate E-MAF’s potential to accelerate polymeric controlled-release system development and drug-delivery industrialization.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nابزار مجازی «ProteinTalks»؛ پیش‌بینی پاسخ‌های دارویی سرطا... (https://www.pezeshk-site.ir/2026/09/12/%D8%A7%D8%A8%D8%B2%D8%A7%D8%B1-%D9%85%D8%AC%D8%A7%D8%B2%DB%8C-proteintalks%D8%9B-%D9%BE%DB%8C%D8%B4%D8%A8%DB%8C%D9%86%DB%8C-%D9%BE%D8%A7%D8%B3%D8%AE%D9%87%D8%A7%DB%8C/)\nciteturn781search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4 days ago; Crawled: 3 days ago; در مورد ProteinTalks، محدودیت‌ها عبارت‌اند از:\n## محدودیت‌ها و نکاتی که باید با احتیاط خواند\n\nهر گزارش علمی باید همراه با آگاهی از محدودیت‌های مطالعه خوانده شود. در مورد ProteinTalks، محدودیت‌ها عبارت‌اند از:\n\n  * استفاده از خطوط سلولی آزمایشگاهی: نتایج مبتنی بر سلول‌های کشت‌شده (in vitro) هستند؛ این محیط‌ها ساده‌تر از تومورهای واقعی در بدن‌اند و فاقد بسیاری از تعاملات بافتی، ایمنی و متابولیک می‌باشند.\n  * عدم تعمیم مستقیم به بیماران: موفقیت در مدل‌های سلولی به معنای مؤثر بودن در بیماران نیست؛ نیاز به مطالعات حیوانی و کارآزمایی‌های بالینی دارد.\n  * وابستگی به داده‌های آموزشی: دقت مدل مستلزم داده‌های باکیفیت، متنوع و نماینده است؛ اگر داده‌ها محدود یا مغرضانه باشند، پیش‌بینی‌ها نیز ممکن است تعمیم‌پذیری ضعیفی داشته باشند.\n  * عدم در نظر گرفتن میکرومحیط تومور: عوامل محیطی مانند سلول‌های ایمنی، رگ‌زایی و بافت همبند در مدل‌های سلولی شبیه‌سازی کامل ندارند.\n  * تفاوت بین ارتباط و علیت: اینکه پروتئینی با مقاومت همبستگی دارد به معنای آن نیست که علت مقاومت است؛ آزمایش‌های مکانیکی و مداخله‌ای لازم است تا رابطه علت و معلولی تایید شود.\n  * نیاز به شفافیت مدل: بسیاری از مدل‌های هوش مصنوعی پیچیده هستند و توضیح‌پذیری (explainability) آن‌ها محدود است؛ برای پذیرش بالینی، درک مکانیسم‌های پیش‌بینی اهمیت دارد.\n\n## آیا این ابزار درمان جدیدی ارائه می‌دهد؟\n\nخیر—گزارش نشان می‌دهد که ProteinTalks یک ابزار پیش‌بینی و اولویت‌بندی تحقیقاتی است، نه یک درمان بالینی جدید. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDevin Voice auf Product Hunt: Fakten zur Veröffentlichung | AIToolly (https://aitoolly.com/de/ai-news/article/2026-09-12-cognition-introduces-devin-voice-on-product-hunt-real-time-spoken-interaction-meets-autonomous-softw)\nciteturn781search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 days ago; Crawled: 3 days ago; # Devin Voice auf Product Hunt gelistet: Neuer Eintrag von KP im September 2026 veröffentlicht\n\nProduktstart Devin Voice Product Hunt Produktstart\n\n# Devin Voice auf Product Hunt gelistet: Neuer Eintrag von KP im September 2026 veröffentlicht\n\nAuf der Plattform Product Hunt wurde ein neuer Eintrag unter der Bezeichnung Devin Voice veröffentlicht. Die Erfassung dieses Eintrags fand am 10. September 2026 um 22:45 Uhr UTC statt und wurde von einer Person mit der Autorenangabe KP vorgenommen. In der zugrunde liegenden Originalmeldung sind abgesehen von diesen primären Metadaten und der offiziellen Produkt-URL keine weiteren textlichen Beschreibungen, Funktionsübersichten oder Dokumentationen enthalten. Dieser Artikel fasst die dokum